The limit is proved in P3 (sparsemax loss is zero exactly on the margin set; Martins & Astudillo 2016 Prop. 3, read in the local copy). Decisive CPU check on the torus position-operator features (512 of the 3,072 instances; truth = 1 nonzero per colour row of a 5×640 rule; predictions written before running):
- lasso, λ=1e-3, converged: 0.914 query exact (6.9 nonzeros per row);
- WTA write + floor, λ=1e-3: 0.914 (1.9 nonzeros per row, closer to the truth); λ=3e-4: 0.912;
- WTA + leak without the floor (η=1e-3, converged, all demo cells won): 0.006;
- min-norm least squares: 0.012.
My prediction for the floorless WTA (0.6-0.9) was wrong. So STDP+WTA cannot be the selection principle where selection matters. 'Competition among synapses needs net depression' (Song, Miller & Abbott 2000; Nessler et al. 2013's −1 depression term in STDP-in-WTA circuits) is the literature reading of keeping a0 < 0.
